id: pm-y4kovm
title: "GH-1048: Windows Node 24 numeric EDQUOT fixtures construct NaN on platforms that do not declare that errno"
description: "Nightly run 31995604146 passed 7,450 tests but failed the two numeric host-errno cases because node:os.constants.errno is platform-specific and EDQUOT is absent on Windows. The runtime map also admitted missing constants as undefined keys. Preserve Linux EDQUOT coverage, select a declared capacity errno per host, and filter missing numeric constants before map construction."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:ci","area:sdk",error-taxonomy,nightly,portability,windows
created_at: "2026-08-17T05:20:21.101Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T05:22:38.276Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T05:22:04.820Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T05:22:04.820Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The runtime numeric errno map contains only integral constants declared by the executing platform; Linux continues to exercise EDQUOT while Windows exercises an equivalent declared capacity errno; Focused and full exact coverage pass and the hosted Windows Node 24 leg is green
parent: pm-3lhth4
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: github-actions
severity: high
environment: "windows-latest, Node 24, Nightly Validation run 31995604146"
repro_steps: Run pnpm test on windows-latest Node 24 at v2026.8.17; observe host-environment-errors.spec.ts and test-command.spec.ts construct errno NaN from absent EDQUOT.
resolution: "Resolved: numeric host-error lookup now admits only integral errno constants declared by the active platform, and capacity-error tests prefer EDQUOT where available with ENOSPC as the portable fallback."
expected_result: Numeric host-errno classification tests use values declared by the executing platform and preserve typed capacity refusals.
actual_result: "Both fixtures constructed Unknown system error -undefined with errno NaN, so classification returned null and the Windows nightly failed after 7,450 passing tests."
affected_version: 2026.8.17
fixed_version: 2026.8.18
component: SDK host-environment boundary and linked-test sandbox
regression: true
customer_impact: No published CLI runtime regression; the nightly portability gate was red and could not validate subsequent releases.
